          "rule_file": "use_exceptions_properly.json",
          "rule_content": {
            "description": "Prefer exceptions over error codes for exceptional conditions. Use exceptions for truly exceptional situations, provide informative error messages, and create domain-specific exception types.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "do": {
                  "description": "Use exceptions for exceptional situations",
                  "content": [
                    "Use exceptions for truly exceptional situations",
                    "Provide informative error messages with context",
                    "Create domain-specific exception types",
                    "Include relevant data in exception objects",
                    "",
                    "Correct Examples (proper exceptions):",
                    "- throw new InvalidOrderException('Order missing required items', {orderId, items})",
                    "- throw new PaymentFailedException('Payment declined', {transactionId, reason})",
                    "- throw new ResourceNotFoundException('User not found', {userId})",
                    "",
                    "Exception Best Practices:",
                    "- Use for truly exceptional conditions (not normal flow)",
                    "- Provide context: what, why, relevant data",
                    "- Create specific exception types for different failures",
                    "- Include actionable information in message",
                    "- Don't expose sensitive data in messages"
                  ]
                },
                "dont": {
                  "description": "Don't use exceptions for normal control flow or return error codes",
                  "content": [
                    "Don't use exceptions for normal control flow",
                    "Don't swallow exceptions silently",
                    "Don't return error codes from modern APIs",
                    "",
                    "Wrong Examples (misused exceptions):",
                    "- try { user = findUser(); } catch { user = createUser(); } // normal flow",
                    "- catch (e) { } // swallowing exception",
                    "- return -1; // error code instead of exception",
                    "- throw new Error('Error') // uninformative message",
                    "",
                    "Exception Misuse Indicators (REFACTOR):",
                    "- Exceptions for expected conditions (empty array, null result)",
                    "- Empty catch blocks silencing errors",
                    "- Generic Error without specific type",
                    "- Error codes (-1, 0, 1) instead of exceptions",
                    "- Exception messages without context",
                    "",
                    "Instead:",
                    "- Use null/optional for 'not found' (expected)",
                    "- Log and/or rethrow exceptions (never swallow)",
                    "- Create specific exception types",
                    "- Include context in error messages",
                    "- Reserve exceptions for truly exceptional cases"
                  ]
                }
              }
            ],
